column2:
Nice thing about this one is that we have the implementation details right in the article:<p><pre><code>    mbedtls_ssl_conf_dh_param_bin(conf, dhm_p, sizeof(dhm_g), dhm_g, sizeof(dhm_g));
</code></pre>
The first sizeof(dhm_g) should have been sizeof(dhm_p).  So, do you attribute this to a simple typo (hard to catch at a glance due to similar letter shapes), "single letter variable names are bad" but the wikipedia page on DH also calls them p and g - it takes a little digging to get that "root" and "modulus" would have been better names, but maybe having them <i>directly</i> match the most common form of the equation would have made them easier to review...<p>Or do you just add it to the list of C crimes, that "passing storage length and pointer" is maybe the worst possible way to return written-to storage from a function :-)
